# Build context is the identity-api Go module root (see Dockerfile).
#
# Two entries here are correctness requirements, not size optimisations:
#
#   internal/db  is sqlc-generated and untracked. Excluding it forces the image to
#                use the code generated inside the build from db/queries and
#                db/migrations, instead of whatever a developer happens to have on
#                disk. A stale local copy would compile cleanly against a schema the
#                image does not ship.
#   .env         holds real local secrets. A COPY . . would bake them into a layer
#                that survives every later instruction, including one that deletes
#                the file.

internal/db/

.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# Host-built artifacts: wrong GOOS, and they would shadow nothing but waste context.
bin/
*.exe
*.out
*.test
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Build definition itself.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
